Here's a C++ function to determine if a given string is a palindrome, **considering only alphanumeric characters and ignoring case**. The function is case-insensitive and ignores non-alphanumeric characters.

### ✅ Function Implementation:

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cctype>

bool isPalindrome(const std::string& str) {
    // Create a new string containing only alphanumeric characters and lowercase
    std::string filtered;
    for (char ch : str) {
        if (std::isalnum(ch)) {
            filtered += std::tolower(ch);
        }
    }

    // Check if the filtered string is a palindrome
    int left = 0;
    int right = filtered.length() - 1;
    while (left < right) {
        if (filtered[left] != filtered[right]) {
            return false;
        }
        left++;
        right--;
    }
    return true;
}
